","It connects to daily life"],"sort_order":174,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-175","prompt":"How can joy and seriousness exist together?","theme":"Joy, Resistance & Collective Change","answers":["Humor","Care","Creativity","Commitment"],"sort_order":175,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-176","prompt":"How can the body participate in resistance without words?","theme":"Joy, Resistance & Collective Change","answers":["Presence","Movement","Refusal","Endurance"],"sort_order":176,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-177","prompt":"What changes when people gather publicly around an issue?","theme":"Joy, Resistance & Collective Change","answers":["It becomes visible","It feels shared","It feels urgent","It feels hopeful"],"sort_order":177,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-178","prompt":"What is a common starting point for everyday resistance?","theme":"Joy, Resistance & Collective Change","answers":["A boundary","A conversation","Mutual aid","A small refusal"],"sort_order":178,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-179","prompt":"Where does sustainable courage usually come from?","theme":"Joy, Resistance & Collective Change","answers":["Community","Preparation","Purpose","Past victories"],"sort_order":179,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-180","prompt":"What makes a movement feel alive?","theme":"Joy, Resistance & Collective Change","answers":["People are learning","People are connecting","People are creating","People are acting"],"sort_order":180,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-181","prompt":"What should a better future give people more of?","theme":"Future Society, Freedom & Human Limits","answers":["Time","Autonomy","Security","Connection"],"sort_order":181,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-182","prompt":"If automation expands, what should society prioritize?","theme":"Future Society, Freedom & Human Limits","answers":["Shorter work hours","Shared wealth","Public services","Education"],"sort_order":182,"version":"classic"},{"id":"classic-183","prompt":"Wh